{"name":"Antique Cameo","hex":"#f0baa4","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"antique","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having existed in ancient times, descended from antiquity; used especially in reference to Greece and Rome.","Belonging to former times, not modern, out of date, old-fashioned."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In general, anything very old; specifically:\n An old object perceived as having value because of its aesthetic or historical significance.","An old object perceived as having value because of its aesthetic or historical significance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/antique"},{"term":"cameo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of jewelry, etc., carved in relief.","A single very brief appearance, especially by a prominent celebrity in a movie or song."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To appear in a cameo role."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cameo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cameo (carving)","blocks":[{"text":"Cameo is a method of carving an object such as an engraved gem, item of jewellery or vessel. It nearly always features a raised (positive) relief image; contrast with intaglio, which has a negative image. Originally, and still in discussing historical work, cameo only referred to works where the relief image was of a contrasting colour to the background; this was achieved by carefully carving a piece of material with a flat plane where two contrasting colours met, removing all the first colour except for the image to leave a contrasting background."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Great_Cameo_of_France_CdM_Paris_Bab264_n1.jpg/330px-Great_Cameo_of_France_CdM_Paris_Bab264_n1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cameo_(carving)","wikidata":"Q28512"},{"title":"Antique","blocks":[{"text":"An antique is an item perceived as having value because of its aesthetic or historical significance, and often defined as at least 100 years old, although the term is often used loosely to describe any object that is old. An antique is usually an item that is collected or desirable because of its age, beauty, rarity, condition, utility, personal emotional connection, or other unique features. It is an object that represents a previous era or time period in human history. Vintage and collectible are used to describe items that are old, but do not meet the 100-year criterion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/06_Restoration_of_gilded_mirror_in_Muzeum_Gornoslaskie%2C_Bytom%2C_Poland_-_furniture_restorer_working.jpg/330px-06_Restoration_of_gilded_mirror_in_Muzeum_Gornoslaskie%2C_Bytom%2C_Poland_-_furniture_restorer_working.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antique","wikidata":"Q472760"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Adlerkameo_KHM.jpg/500px-Adlerkameo_KHM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Adlerkameo_KHM.jpg/1280px-Adlerkameo_KHM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Adlerkameo_KHM.jpg/500px-Adlerkameo_KHM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eagle Cameo, Roman 27 B.C. Two-layered onyx.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAdlerkameo_KHM.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Cameo_August_BM_Gem3577.jpg/500px-Cameo_August_BM_Gem3577.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Cameo_August_BM_Gem3577.jpg/1280px-Cameo_August_BM_Gem3577.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont